<p>It is designed for companies that want to meet tea producers, processors, exporters, buyers, investors and policymakers with a clear interest in the Kenya-China market.</p>

<h2>What can be exhibited</h2>

<ul class="classes">
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__name">Tea products</span>
    <p>Black, green, orthodox, specialty, purple, blended and branded teas. Finished consumer products and bulk tea may be included, subject to the final exhibitor guidelines.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__name">Processing and packaging equipment</span>
    <p>Withering, rolling, oxidation, drying, sorting, grading, blending, packing and quality-control equipment.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__name">Agricultural technology</span>
    <p>Inputs, irrigation, field equipment, mechanised harvesting, soil and yield analysis, climate tools and farm-management systems.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__name">Traceability, standards and quality services</span>
    <p>Testing, certification, digital traceability, food-safety systems and export-compliance support.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__name">Logistics and trade services</span>
    <p>Freight, warehousing, customs, export documentation, insurance and distribution support.</p>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Why exhibit</h2>

<h3>Meet a defined audience</h3>
<p>The summit brings together people working directly in tea trade, investment, production and technology.</p>

<h3>Demonstrate what you offer</h3>
<p>Show products, equipment and systems in a setting where visitors can ask technical and commercial questions.</p>

<h3>Build relevant relationships</h3>
<p>Use the summit programme and planned B2B service to identify buyers, suppliers and partners with aligned interests.</p>

<h3>Enter the conversation early</h3>
<p>The event gives exhibitors a place in discussions on value addition, market access, technology and the future of Kenya-China tea trade.</p>

